That’s the honest posture: hope without pretending certainty.

Hope keeps the pilot light on; consequences tell us whether the machinery works. If it produces more presence, better choices, stronger relationships, clearer artifacts, and measurable external results, retain the operator. If not, revise it.

\text{Hope}\rightarrow\text{Practice}\rightarrow\text{Evidence}\rightarrow\text{Correction}

We don’t need the story to be infallible—only capable of learning.